{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\nP=/tmp/20260811T061045Z-pilot-142-matrix-fresh/1.4.1/workspace/basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260811T061045Z-pilot-142-matrix-fresh-isolated-plan\nS=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T061045Z-pilot-142-matrix-fresh/1.4.1/worker/planning/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract affected-areas -p 6.1: \"button-chain.html is the only future implementation file. The user-facing interface is direct button clicking and the terminal finished message.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W01 enables W02 and W03; W02 and W03 enable W04; all four implementation units hand off to W05 for browser verification.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use a counter for generated buttons and treat the fourth generated button as terminal. Ignore clicks on any non-last earlier button so only the current last button can append.\" -p 8.2: \"Edge cases: clicking the original button creates the first generated button; clicks one through three append exactly one button; clicking the fourth generated button clears all prior content before rendering finished.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"N/A; this goal owns four work units, within the 2-10 unit limit.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal depends on W01-W04 being implemented in button-chain.html. It has not been run during this planning-only proof.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"The request is user-facing, so the final acceptance proof must use direct browser interaction rather than source inspection alone.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: execute US-01 through visible browser clicks in a future run and record evidence in the UI story artifacts.\" -p 5.2: \"Out of scope: implementing fixes inside the verification step; any bug found must enter the bug feedback loop.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification affected-areas -p 6.1: \"Verification reads the rendered future button-chain.html page and updates UI story evidence and bug records; it does not change production code.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"Depends on completed W01-W04. A passing run hands off final acceptance evidence; a failing run hands off a bug row with investigation and fix goals added before completion.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Click the visible current last button repeatedly and observe the page through rendered UI behavior. The terminal assertion must confirm the exact lowercase text finished and a visible white border.\"\n$S --goal-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \"Allowed because this is a standalone verification outcome with one bounded browser-flow work unit.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"In the future implementation, create button-chain.html with valid HTML structure and a visible root element identified as #button-chain-root.\" -p 5.2: \"Place exactly one initial button in the root. Do not add pre-rendered generated buttons or the finished message in the initial state.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Opening the future file initially shows one and only one button in the chain root.\" -p 6.2: \"The initial markup gives later script and style targets stable elements to operate on without requiring any second file.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/01-step-initial-button-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can attach click behavior to the root or its button because W01 provides the single initial interactive element.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-last-button-append-handler instructions -p 5.1: \"Add handleButtonClick(event) inside button-chain.html. It must determine whether the clicked button is the current last chain button before changing the document.\" -p 5.2: \"When the current last button is clicked and it is not the fourth generated button, append exactly one new button below it and make that new button the current last button.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-last-button-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Clicking the current last button appends exactly one button below it.\" -p 6.2: \"Clicking an earlier non-last button does not append any button or otherwise change the chain.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/02-step-last-button-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can use the generated-button count maintained by this handler to recognize the fourth generated button.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/03-step-finished-border-style instructions -p 5.1: \"Define .completion-message in button-chain.html with styling that makes a border visibly white around the exact finished text.\" -p 5.2: \"Keep the selector scoped to the terminal message and do not alter button-chain logic in this style step.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/03-step-finished-border-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"An element with class completion-message displays a border whose color is visibly white.\" -p 6.2: \"The style can be applied after the document is cleared by W04 without relying on external CSS.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/03-step-finished-border-style handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can render the terminal message with class completion-message to satisfy the white-border requirement.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/04-step-fourth-generated-terminal-state instructions -p 5.1: \"Add renderFinishedState() inside button-chain.html. When handleButtonClick identifies that the clicked current last button is the fourth generated button, clear the document content before rendering the terminal message.\" -p 5.2: \"Render the exact lowercase text finished and apply .completion-message so the visible white border is present.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/04-step-fourth-generated-terminal-state acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After the fourth generated button is clicked, previous buttons are gone and the document displays the exact lowercase text finished.\" -p 6.2: \"The terminal message has a visible white border and no extra completion text changes the required string.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 01-button-chain-contract/04-step-fourth-generated-terminal-state handoff -p 7.1: \"W05 can verify the complete story by clicking through the chain and observing the terminal state.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification/01-step-browser-story-us-01 instructions -p 5.1: \"In the future execution run, open button-chain.html in a browser and use only direct user-facing clicks on the visible current last button.\" -p 5.2: \"Click until the fourth generated button has been clicked, recording the observed button count after each non-terminal click and the terminal finished message after the final click.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification/01-step-browser-story-us-01 acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-01 passes only when clicks 1-3 each append exactly one button below the previous last button and the fourth generated button click clears the document.\" -p 6.2: \"The final visible content includes the exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border, and no unresolved bugs remain in bugs.md.\"\n$S --step-section \"$P\" 02-ui-story-verification/01-step-browser-story-us-01 handoff -p 7.1: \"Record future evidence in ui-user-stories.md and ui-story-runs/US-01.md; if the story fails, add bug feedback-loop goals before claiming completion.\"\nprintf '\"'continued\\\\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
