{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260811T061045Z-pilot-142-matrix-fresh-isolated-plan/adversarial-review.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review\n\n## Verdict\n\nNot approved. The plan stays inside the planning-only boundary, but it has unresolved decomposition and behavior-contract gaps that would make future execution ambiguous.\n\n## Findings\n\n### AR-01 - Unregistered W06 step breaks work-unit ownership\n\n`01-button-chain-contract/steps/05-step-implementation-contract-check.md` owns `W06`, but `W06` is absent from `work-unit-inventory.md`, absent from `01-button-chain-contract/goal.md` owned work units, and absent from `01-button-chain-contract/progress.md`. This violates the one-to-one inventory/goal/step mapping and creates an unplanned verification step.\n\nRequired fix: either remove `01-button-chain-contract/steps/05-step-implementation-contract-check.md`, or add `W06` consistently to `work-unit-inventory.md`, `01-button-chain-contract/goal.md`, `01-button-chain-contract/progress.md`, and any required testing companion/progress tracking.\n\n### AR-02 - Browser story under-clicks the required terminal state\n\nThe task says pressing the fourth generated button clears the document. Starting from one initial button, that requires five user clicks: initial button creates generated 1, then generated 1 creates generated 2, generated 2 creates generated 3, generated 3 creates generated 4, and pressing generated 4 clears. `ui-user-stories.md` and `ui-story-runs/US-01.md` instead say to click the current last button four times, which would stop at creation of the fourth generated button rather than pressing it.\n\nRequired fix: update `ui-user-stories.md`, `ui-story-runs/US-01.md`, `work-unit-inventory.md` W05 if needed, and `02-ui-story-verification/steps/01-step-browser-story-us-01.md` so the browser flow explicitly performs five direct clicks and distinguishes the fourth generated button press from the earlier append clicks.\n\n### AR-03 - Terminal behavior modifies an unowned symbol\n\n`01-button-chain-contract/steps/04-step-fourth-generated-terminal-state.md` is scoped to `renderFinishedState()`, but its instructions require `handleButtonClick(event)` to identify the fourth generated button and call the terminal renderer. That means W04 needs to change the handler symbol owned by W02, or W02 must already include a planned terminal-branch handoff. As written, the terminal-state work cannot be implemented atomically inside only `renderFinishedState()`.\n\nRequired fix: revise `work-unit-inventory.md` and the affected step files so the fourth-generated branch in `handleButtonClick(event)` is explicitly owned. Acceptable repairs include adding a separate handler-branch work unit, or moving the terminal dispatch responsibility into W02 while leaving W04 limited to rendering.\n\n## Boundary Check\n\nNo HTML creation, HTML inspection, browser run, server start, driver use, or unrelated repository/history access is required by the reviewed plan artifacts. Bug recovery is planned through `bugs.md`, `bug-register.md`, and the verification goal, but the findings above must be resolved before execution readiness.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
